.TH NEO-SETTINGS 1 "2026-11-12" "gnome-phone 0.1.1" "GNOME Phone"
.SH NAME
neo-settings \- settings app for GNOME Phone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neo-settings
.RB [ \-\-page
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-app
.IR desktop-id ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Neo Settings is the phone's Settings app: connections, sounds, notifications, display, battery, wallpaper, the home
screen, the lock screen, location, accounts, apps, language, date and time, accessibility and the phone's details.
It answers GNOME Settings' "launch-panel" action under its own name, so GNOME Phone opens it wherever GNOME would open
a Settings panel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " name"
Opens one page: for example home, wallpaper, wifi, bluetooth, mobile, sound, notifications, display, battery,
lockscreen, location, accounts, apps, language, datetime, accessibility or about. GNOME Settings' panel names work too.
.TP
.BI \-\-app " desktop-id"
Opens one app's page (its notifications, permissions and default handlers).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/neo-keyring-rekey
Gives the login keyring the new lock-screen password when the PIN, pattern or password changes.
.SH SEE ALSO
neo-launcher(1)
